{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "nr-railroad-support-nation",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.5 step 7e: the `nr-railroad-support-nation` RunSpec computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE -- the nation, August 2020, weekday, sector 12 (Railroad Support), onroad diesel, CO, NOx, SO2 and PM10. NONROAD's whole inventory at the nation: 1,119 equipment points, 5,777 cohorts, 23,108 rows, every key right and the shape recomputed.\n\nALL 23,108 ROWS REPRODUCE: 23,104 cells at the full 2e-5 gate, and one cohort's four under a declared `cell_exception` in tolerance.toml (PLAN.md §7.3.38). Every GASOLINE SO2 cell was 1.38e-4 high until the sulfur was read as NONROAD reads it: `rdnropt.f` takes `line(21:30)` with F10.0, so MOVES's `0.00066419` arrives as `0.0006641` (`opt_option_value`, measured in the run's own NONROAD worker folder: MOVES's output equals NONROAD's `Output.tbl` in every cell). What is left is diesel 2270002066 model year 2010, 0.7 to 1.3e-4 off in all four pollutants: the 75-100 hp point's base-year population. MOVES sums the states in binary64 to 137670.538 and the `.POP` file prints 137670.5; this document sums them in binary32 to 137670.547, which prints .6, and agedist.f's newest-cohort residual for 2010 is a cancellation (1.32300 - 1.32201) that turns the 7e-7 into 2.4e-4 (NONROAD.BMY and the instrumented AGEDIST trace both show it). Forcing the rounding to .5 closes the cohort to 1.6e-5. Summing in binary64 needs an explicit binary64-to-binary32 conversion, which the format does not have (esm-spec 11.3.1 refuses the mixed equation; EarthSciML/EarthSciAST#536), so tolerance.toml holds that one cohort to 2e-4 with the measurement written out.\n\nThe two folds `nr-commercial-nation` could not see -- the growth pattern's minimum over states and `nrUSMonthAllocation` -- this run's oracle does see, and it found the SEASON file's printed month fractions (PLAN.md §7.3.37) and the two residuals above."
  },
  "domain": {
    "element_type": "Float32"
  },
